  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The volume of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCl</mi></math>, containing <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>73</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, required to completely neutralise <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaOH</mi></math> obtained by reacting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>69</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of metallic sodium with water, is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>mL</mi></math>. (Nearest Integer)</p><p>(Given : molar Masses of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Na</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Cl</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>23</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>35</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> respectively)</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "15",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Mole of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaOH</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>69</mn></mrow><mn>23</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>Na</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#10230;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>NaOH</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>Number of moles of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Na</mi></math> = Number of moles of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaOH</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaOH</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>HCl</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>NaCl</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p><p>Moles of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCl</mi></math>&nbsp;= moles of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaOH</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mtext>Molarity</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mi>HCl</mi></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></math>Number of moles of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaOH</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mn>73</mn><mrow><mn>36</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>03</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Lit</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
  }
